# What the sanitizer MUST print when tests/asan-canary/main.zen is built
# with the sweep's own flags and run. One substring per line; `#` is a
# comment and a blank line is ignored. EVERY line here has to appear in
# the program's stderr or scripts/asan_corpus.sh refuses to run the
# sweep -- see that script's header, and main.zen's.
#
# It is the REPORT that is asserted, not the exit status. A program can
# exit non-zero for a dozen reasons that have nothing to do with a
# sanitizer being wired up, and every one of them would read as a
# healthy canary.
AddressSanitizer: stack-use-after-return
